0", "type": "B"}], "sessionCode": "1", "sessionBeginDt": "09/02/2020", "sessionEndDt": "12/21/2020", "sessionLong": "Regular Academic Session", "exploreCriteriaIds": null}], "description": "We stand on one side of a growing crevasse that separates \"us\" who know about climate change from \"those others,\" who did not know.\u00a0 This course will deploy works of literature and cinema (primarily from the Romance languages) to think about the unique disruptions to embedded narratives; to develop tools and vocabulary for reading under the sign of climate emergency.\u00a0 Discussions will be in English.\u00a0 Students are encouraged to read in the original if possible.\u00a0 Authors may include: Antonioni, Calvino, Martel, Perec, Schweblin, Verne and Zola.\u00a0 Topics may include: Historiography, archives, mourning/solastalgia, scale, desertification and the model of compound interest in relation to narrative.\u00a0 Take-home writing assignments and seminar/research paper are required.\u00a0", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Fall.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "GR", "acadGroup": "AS", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": null}, {"strm": 2769, "crseId": 368458, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "ROMS", "catalogNbr": "6650", "titleShort": "Revolution:Intellectual Histor", "titleLong": "Revolution: An Intellectual History", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "001", "classNbr": 17028, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "03:00PM", "timeEnd": "04:55PM", "startDt": "09/02/2020", "endDt": "12/16/2020", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 1, "netid": "vt225", "firstName": "Enzo", "middleName": "", "lastName": "Traverso"}], "pattern": "T", "facilityDescr": "Online Meeting", "bldgDescr": "Virtual", "facilityDescrshort": "Online", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [{"classNotesSeq": 1, "descrlong": "Conducted in English."}], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "09/02/2020", "endDt": "12/21/2020", "addConsent": "N", "addConsentDescr": "No Special Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [], "instructionMode": "OL", "instrModeDescrshort": "OL", "instrModeDescr": "Online", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "O", "exploreCriteriaIds": null, "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 4, "unitsMaximum": 4, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["LEC"], "gradingBasis": "OPT", "gradingBasisShort": "Stdnt Opt", "gradingBasisLong": "Letter or S/U grades", "simpleCombinations": [{"subject": "HIST", "catalogNbr": "6655", "type": "C"}], "sessionCode": "1", "sessionBeginDt": "09/02/2020", "sessionEndDt": "12/21/2020", "sessionLong": "Regular Academic Session", "exploreCriteriaIds": null}], "description": "For more than two centuries, revolutions have marked the rhythm of modernity.\u00a0 In 1780, the original meaning of revolution - an astronomical rotation - was transformed in order to apprehend a social and political overthrow.\u00a0 This course will investigate the multiple uses of this crucial concept of political theory, from the revolutionary canon (Blanqui, Marx, Fanon...) to the classics of conservatism (Maistre, Cort\u00e9s, Schmitt...), which depict contemporary history as a conflict between revolutions and counter-revolutions, socialist and fascist revolutions.\u00a0 We will explore the connections between history and theory, and stress the global dimension of revolutions, forged by a permanent transfer of ideas and people from one continent to another.", "catalogBread